# Wave W17-W (Mt. Apex — South): step stone — dressed front-hall stone with door-jamb banding: warm ashlar courses carrying two pale vertical jamb bands, the dressed doorways of the west and south doors repeated in the wall’s own drawing (design: the mountain’s front hall, two dressed-stone doors). Mt. Apex — South’s own wall — split from Central’s spine stone by the jamb bands and the warmth (doors vs gallery) and from North’s zenith stone by value entire: the hall is lamplit mid-warm, the top floor is sky-pale.
